    "bio": "Muthuthanthrige Vishwa Thilina Fernando, born on September 18, 1991, in Colombo, Sri Lanka, is a professional left-arm medium-fast bowler who represents the national side in all three formats. He made his Test debut for Sri Lanka on August 4, 2016, against Australia in Galle, taking a wicket in his first over. A significant highlight of his career includes a crucial 78-run last-wicket partnership with Kusal Perera in 2019, leading Sri Lanka to a historic one-wicket victory against South Africa. He also emerged as the highest wicket-taker in that series with 12 wickets at an average of 18.91."
